------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Karpathy coding guidelines
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The `np-kb-coding-rules` skill adapts behavioral coding guidelines originally
published as "andrej-karpathy-skills" (multica-ai/andrej-karpathy-skills),
MIT License. nervepack condensed them into native coding rules, reorganized the
structure, and extended them with nervepack-specific rules.
Source: https://github.com/multica-ai/andrej-karpathy-skills

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
designer-skills (design process sequence)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The `np-flow-design` skill's sequence (mode, interrogate, brief, tokens, build,
review), its `.design/<feature>/` artifact layout, and the review checklist and
severity buckets in `np-kb-design-critique` adapt material from
"designer-skills" (julianoczkowski/designer-skills), Apache License 2.0.
nervepack condensed eight skills into one flow, replaced the browser-only
capture step with a per-surface table, and added the Flutter arm.
Source: https://github.com/julianoczkowski/designer-skills

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
impeccable (design vocabulary and modes)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The `np-flow-design` skill's four surface modes (Persuade, Operate, Read,
Experience), its steering-verb table, the brief-wins and refinement-versus-
redesign rules, and the bounded-verification rule adapt material from
"impeccable" (pbakaus/impeccable), Apache License 2.0. nervepack took the
vocabulary and the rules only; none of the project's scripts, hooks, CLI, or
PRODUCT.md / DESIGN.md artifact machinery is used.
Source: https://github.com/pbakaus/impeccable

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
material-3-skill (Material Design 3 roles)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The Material 3 color-role vocabulary and the component name mapping in
`np-kb-flutter-ui-design` adapt material from "material-3-skill"
(hamen/material-3-skill), MIT License.
Source: https://github.com/hamen/material-3-skill

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
superpowers (process workflow patterns)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
nervepack's process expectations (explore-before-build, test-first, root-cause
debugging, plan execution) are designed to compose with the "superpowers" Claude
Code plugin when it is installed. nervepack does not vendor or depend on it; it is
referenced as an optional companion process toolkit.
Source: https://github.com/obra/superpowers

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
mermaid (vendored diagram renderer)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
dashboard/vendor/mermaid.min.js is the mermaid diagramming library, MIT License,
vendored verbatim so the dashboard renders Mermaid diagrams client-side without
any external/CDN fetch (the dashboard's no-external-fetch invariant). Loaded only
on wiki pages that contain a diagram; gated by the evaluator.wiki_mermaid param.
Source: https://github.com/mermaid-js/mermaid
